## What to delete / converge (in `ZLinkManagedMeshNode.cs`, `ZLinkMeshPeerAdmission.cs`, `ZLinkMeshPeer.cs`)
1. Reciprocal settlement: `BeginReciprocalHandoverSettlement`, `ObserveReciprocalHandoverDisconnect`, the lane disconnect mask
   (`ReciprocalHandoverPending/DisconnectMask/RetiredDirection/RetiredEndpoint` on the peer), and the deferred `Admitted`
   publication. Publish `Admitted` as soon as the logical survivor is selected (as cpp `service_topology_registry.cpp:281-309`
   and node `raw-service-mesh-runtime.ts:740-767` do). The losing direction's in-flight request timing out once is the
   contract; the durable-operation replay policy (04-actor-model sender bullets) covers the resend.
2. Physical pair re-pin and pair-based ingress fence: `_transportPairsByRid` rewrites in `CompletePeerAdmissionUnderLock` and
   the ready handler, `_readyOutboundEndpoints`/`_readyInboundRids` as admission inputs, the `HasCurrentInfrastructureControlSource`
   / `HasCurrentApplicationSource` pair veto on received records (`:5128-5192`, `:5586-5605`), and the reply pair epoch
   invalidation (`_nativeReplyEpochsByTransportPair`, `:6133-6153`, `:8895-8976`, `:10437-10455`). Routed receive is identified
   by the logical RID; Core owns physical pipe selection (05-transport-liveness as amended in `3a2ada8187`: connection_id is
   diagnostic only). Keep monitor observation for readiness/liveness only.
3. `RetireDuplicatePeer`'s physical retirement decisions (which endpoint/RID to disconnect to make Core pick a survivor): remove;
   Core already collapsed the duplicate. Keep the framework's logical duplicate bookkeeping (one ready logical peer,
   `NotRequired` handling) — that is framework-owned.
4. `ebff5b3e1b` inbound-intent reuse in `ConnectPeer`: remove (mixed manual/automatic duplicates converge through the
   ordinary duplicate admission, topology spec :688-700), unless the pair-fence removal above does not by itself make
   TicTacToe's JoinGameNotify path pass — in that case STOP and report the trace (do not keep the reuse as a fix).
KEEP: the unilateral Hello outbound fallback (`FindReadyOutboundCandidate` may stay only if it no longer reads a
monitor-derived pair index; otherwise re-express it over the connection candidate registry like cpp
`raw_mesh_connection_candidates_t::for_handshake`), the `DisconnectTransport` endpoint-vs-RID ownership rule, descriptor /
generation admission fences, liveness deadlines, the DEALER-ownership fixture fix.

